@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-json-pointer-resolution-is-strict-own-members-only-canonical-array-indexes
+type: decision-log
+title: "JSON Pointer resolution is strict: own members only, canonical array indexes"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Later features build on `resolvePointer`, and the library must follow the published standard.
+
+## Decision
+
+- A pointer that is neither empty nor starting with `/`, or that has a `~` not followed by `0` or `1`, is invalid and throws.
+- Object members resolve only if they are own properties, so `/__proto__` or `/constructor` never reach the prototype chain.
+- Array tokens must be canonical decimal indexes (no sign, no leading zeros) within range; `-` (past the end) does not resolve and throws.
+- A step into a primitive or `null` throws.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Callers can rely on a thrown error meaning "no such value"; a member whose value is `null` or falsy still resolves.
